{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggDNu1qrVxWtupwv59kn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it. `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, so no grosz is lost.\n\n**The bug:** `split_cents` in `money.py` gave everyone `total // people` and threw away the remainder.\n\n**The fix:** it now uses `divmod` to get both the even share and what's left over. The first `remainder` people each pay one extra grosz, so the shares always add up to the total and differ by at most one grosz.\n\n**Tests:** I added two tests to `test_money.py`:\n- the 1 zł split three ways returns `[34, 33, 33]`\n- for every total from 0 to 249 grosze and every group of 1 to 7 people, the shares add up to the total and differ by at most one grosz\n\nBoth failed before the fix. All 5 tests pass now.\n\nThe extra grosz always goes to the first people in the list. If you'd rather choose who pays it (for example, whoever ordered the most), that would need a small API change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":527,"cache_read_input_tokens":19181,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":527},"output_tokens":313,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7edfda8-6919-42cd-a1da-26539ae45d3c","uuid":"e2d97507-be53-4eec-bee3-06d98011d783","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:15:25.659Z","request_id":"req_011CggDNtmD2nEeH9EetpeKd"}
